  "exec_summary": "The European Union's Markets in Crypto-Assets regulation, known as MiCA, has introduced significant regulatory developments, including restrictions on Belarusian control of MiCA firms, which may impact the compliance landscape for crypto-asset service providers. In Belgium, financial institutions should be aware of the potential implications of MiCA on their operations, particularly with regards to third-tier exchanges. The European Central Bank has also released its Consumer Expectations Survey results for June 2026, which may inform regulatory priorities and supervisory actions. The ECB's survey results may be relevant to Belgian financial institutions in terms of understanding consumer expectations and behaviors in the context of regulatory compliance.",
